<section class="public-page-hero policy-hero"><span class="section-kicker">USING HEALTHTRACK</span><h1>Terms &<br />conditions.</h1><p>A clear guide to using this HealthTrack installation responsibly.</p><span class="policy-date">Last updated: 22 October 2026 · Local demonstration edition</span></section>
<div class="policy-layout public-section"><nav class="policy-nav" aria-label="Terms sections"><a href="#terms-service">The service</a><a href="#terms-account">Your account</a><a href="#terms-content">Your information</a><a href="#terms-use">Acceptable use</a><a href="#terms-guidance">Fitness guidance</a><a href="#terms-availability">Availability</a><a href="#terms-contact">Questions</a></nav><article class="policy-content">
<section id="terms-service"><h2>1. About the service</h2><p>HealthTrack provides workout, meal and measurement tracking, trainer-created plans, progress views, appointment coordination and in-app reminders. This installation is a local coursework demonstration. It does not offer paid subscriptions, payment processing or a native mobile application.</p></section>
<section id="terms-account"><h2>2. Your account</h2><p>Use your own account and keep your password private. Provide accurate information for the features you use. Public registration creates a client account; trainer accounts and assignments are managed by the administrator.</p><p>Do not share credentials or access another person's account. If you think someone has accessed your account, change your password and contact the operator.</p></section>
<section id="terms-content"><h2>3. Your information and contributions</h2><p>You are responsible for the information you enter, including workout logs, meal details, measurements and appointment notes. Only enter information you are entitled to provide. Avoid putting unrelated sensitive information into free-text fields.</p><p>Your entries are used to provide the application's tracking and coordination features. See the <a href="/Home/Privacy">privacy policy</a> for stored information, access rules and available controls. These terms do not grant other users unrestricted access to your records.</p></section>
<section id="terms-use"><h2>4. Acceptable use</h2><ul><li>Use HealthTrack for its intended personal fitness and coordination purposes.</li><li>Respect other users and keep appointment notes and feedback relevant.</li><li>Do not attempt to bypass permissions, interfere with the service or introduce malicious content.</li><li>Do not upload or enter content that you do not have permission to use.</li></ul><p>Administrators can deactivate accounts and manage trainer assignments. Contact the operator if you need help with an account restriction.</p></section>
<section id="terms-guidance"><h2>5. Fitness information and appointments</h2><p>HealthTrack is not a medical device, diagnostic service or substitute for advice from a qualified healthcare professional. Activity and nutrition summaries depend on the data entered and may be incomplete. No particular health, fitness or weight outcome is promised.</p><p>Appointment requests are not confirmed until the relevant provider or coordinator accepts them. Check the appointment status before relying on a booking. Reminders appear in the application; external email and SMS delivery are not enabled in this installation.</p></section>
<section id="terms-availability"><h2>6. Availability and account closure</h2><p>The demonstration may be changed, restarted or unavailable while the operator maintains it. It is not an emergency or time-critical service. There is no guaranteed availability or response time.</p><p>You can stop using your account at any time. Contact the operator about deactivation, export or erasure requests; these are not automatic account features. Deactivation by itself does not erase stored records.</p></section>
<section id="terms-contact"><h2>7. Questions and updates</h2><p>For questions about this installation or these terms, visit <a href="/Home/Contact">Contact us</a>. Changes to this page will be accompanied by an updated date. The operator must supply organization details and terms appropriate to the deployment before offering a public production service.</p></section>
</article></div>
